{"name":"Big Yellow Taxi","hex":"#ffff33","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"big","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Biangai."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of great size, large.","Fat."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/big"},{"term":"yellow","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of sunflower petals and lemons; the color obtained by mixing green and red light, or by subtracting blue from white light; the color evoked by light of wavelength around 580 nm; one of the three primary colors in subtractive color systems.","The middle light in a set of three traffic lights, the lighting of which indicates that drivers should stop short of the intersection if it is safe to do so."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellow hue.","Lacking courage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yellow"},{"term":"taxi","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A vehicle, usually a car, that may be hired for single journeys by members of the public, particularly one with an automated meter to calculate the fare.","An aircraft used for practicing ground manoeuvres."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move an aircraft on the ground under its own power.","To travel by taxicab."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/taxi"}],"entries":[{"title":"Big Yellow Taxi","blocks":[{"text":"\"Big Yellow Taxi\" is a song written, composed, and originally recorded by Canadian singer-songwriter Joni Mitchell in 1970, and originally released on her third album, Ladies of the Canyon (1970). Released in April 1970 by Reprise Records, the single was a hit in her native Canada as well as Australia and on the UK Singles Chart. It only reached No. 67 on the US Billboard Hot 100 in 1970, but was later a bigger hit there for her in a live version released in 1974, which peaked at No. 24. Charting versions have also been recorded by the Neighborhood, and most notably by Amy Grant in 1995 and Counting Crows and Vanessa Carlton in 2002. The song was also sampled in Janet Jackson's \"Got 'til It's Gone\" (1997)."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/59/Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Joni_Mitchell_1970_Canadian_vinyl.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Yellow_Taxi","wikidata":"Q2732732"},{"title":"Yellow cab","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow cab taxicab operators exist all around the world. The original Yellow Cab Company, based in Chicago, Illinois, was one of the largest taxicab companies in the United States."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/New_York_City_taxi_cabs.JPG/330px-New_York_City_taxi_cabs.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow_cab","wikidata":"Q3572121"},{"title":"Taxi","blocks":[{"text":"A taxi, also known as a taxicab or simply a cab, is a vehicle for hire that provides point-to-point transportation for passengers typically on an exclusive, non-shared basis. This differs from public transport, where pick-up and drop-off points are set by the service provider, although demand-responsive transport and share taxis provide hybrid bus/taxi modes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/TAXI.jpg/330px-TAXI.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taxi","wikidata":"Q82650"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg/500px-Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg/1280px-Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/aa/Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg/500px-Joni_Mitchell_1983.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joni Mitchell (pictured in 1983) wrote and recorded the song \"Big Yellow Taxi\".","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoni_Mitchell_1983.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/74/Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png/250px-Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/74/Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/74/Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png/250px-Big_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABig_Yellow_Taxi_by_Amy_Grant_US_single.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/BYTCounting_Crows.jpg/250px-BYTCounting_Crows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/BYTCounting_Crows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9d/BYTCounting_Crows.jpg/250px-BYTCounting_Crows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABYTCounting_Crows.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg/500px-Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg/1280px-Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg/500px-Joni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Joni Mitchell Cup initiated by Club Captain Barry Thomas - co- winners Kevin Dunn and Regan Miles. ","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoni_Mitchell_cup_Barry_Thomas_photo_24_Dec_2024.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Taksi.jpg/500px-Taksi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Taksi.jpg/500px-Taksi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"One of the historical yellow taxis in Baku, Azerbaijan, that were replaced with violet c